# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the leo-study-web project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package (version ^1.6.1) to the project dependencies
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the new dependency and its transitive dependencies

### 2. Modified Files

#### `package.json`
- Added `"@vercel/analytics": "^1.6.1"` to the dependencies section

#### `src/App.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component in the main App component, placed immediately after the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component

## Implementation Details

This React + Vite application follows the standard React implementation pattern for Vercel Web Analytics. The `Analytics` component was added to the main App component to ensure it tracks all page views and user interactions across the entire application.

The component placement is consistent with the existing Vercel Speed Insights integration, ensuring both analytics and performance monitoring are properly configured.

## Framework
- Framework: React 19.2.0 with Vite 7.3.1
- Implementation: Used the `@vercel/analytics/react` package for React applications
- Route Support: The Analytics component automatically integrates with the existing react-router-dom setup for proper route tracking

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed without issues
✅ No new linting errors introduced
✅ All changes are minimal and focused on the specific requirement

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The Analytics will automatically start tracking visitors and page views
2. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. Custom events can be added later if needed using the track() function from @vercel/analytics

## Notes

- The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics documentation for React applications
- No configuration is required; the Analytics component will work automatically when deployed to Vercel
- The component will only send data in production environments by default
